<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:8.5pt;margin-right:16.45pt;margi=
n-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>The Department of Anthropology of=
fers a
graduate program leading to the Master of Arts degree in Anthropology. The
program includes elements of all four subfields of anthropology and
acknowledges their importance, though our faculty strengths are in archaeol=
ogy,
cultural anthropology, and biological anthropology. The department follows =
an
apprenticeship model, and thus the MA student works directly under the
supervision of their graduate advisor. Students are informed of who their
graduate advisor is when they are admitted to the program. Visit the </span=
><b
style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Gill Sans=
 MT",sans-serif;
mso-hansi-font-family:"Trebuchet MS";mso-font-width:110%'>Faculty Page<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:-.05pt'> </span></span></b><span style=3D'mso-font-=
width:
110%'>for the UCF Department of Anthropology for more information about our
faculty. Students in the program are prepared to enter doctoral programs or
begin professional careers following the MA degree.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.4pt;margin-right:11.1pt;margin=
-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.7pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:111%'><span
style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>Degree-seeking students in the Anthropology MA
program may elect to follow either a thesis or non-thesis plan of study. Ea=
ch
plan of study<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>requires<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>a<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt=
'> </span>minimum<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>of<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45p=
t'> </span>30<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>credit<span style=3D'letter-spacing:=
.45pt'> </span>hours,<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>15<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45p=
t'> </span>of<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>which<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.=
45pt'> </span>must<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>be<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45p=
t'> </span>at<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>the<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45=
pt'> </span>6000-level.<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>The<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45=
pt'> </span>thesis<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>option<span style=3D'letter-spacing:=
.45pt'> </span>is<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>designed<span style=3D'letter-spacin=
g:.45pt'>
</span>for<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>students<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.45pt'> </span>who plan to enter doctoral programs,=
 while
the non-thesis option is more appropriate for students entering or continui=
ng
profession careers following the MA degree.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:11.1pt;margin=
-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>The anthropology faculty conduct
research in many geographical areas including Bolivia, Colombia, Egypt,
Guatemala, Mexico, Peru, the Philippines, Turkey, the United States and var=
ious
other locations in the Caribbean and Europe. The department also has multip=
le
research facilities on the Orlando campus that including the following: an
archaeology lab specializing in lithic and ceramic analysis, a forensic
anthropology lab, a paleoethnobotany archaeology lab, a bioarchaeological
sciences lab, an isotope geochemistry and zooarchaeology<span style=3D'lett=
er-spacing:
.55pt'> </span>lab,<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>and<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>an<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55p=
t'> </span>interdisciplinary<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.65pt'> </span>geospatial<span style=3D'letter-spac=
ing:
.55pt'> </span>science<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>lab.<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>Students<span style=3D'letter-spacin=
g:.55pt'>
</span>may<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>have<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>the<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55=
pt'> </span>opportunity<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>to<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55p=
t'> </span>conduct<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>research<span style=3D'letter-spacin=
g:.55pt'>
</span>projects in the various countries or research facilities as part of
their program.</span></p>

