t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>Big Data Analytics, Statistics tr=
ack,
will train researchers with a strong statistics background to analyze massi=
ve,
structured or unstructured data to uncover hidden patterns, unknown
correlations and other useful information that can be used to make better <=
span
style=3D'letter-spacing:-.1pt'>decisions.</span></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:8.9pt;margin-=
bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>The track will provide a strong
foundation in statistical theory and the major methodologies associated with
Big Data Analytics such as predictive analytics, data mining, text analytics
and statistical analysis with an interdisciplinary component that combines =
the
strength of statistics and computer science. It will focus on statistical
theory in addition to statistical computing, statistical data mining and<sp=
an
style=3D'letter-spacing:2.0pt'> </span>their application to business, socia=
l, and
health problems complemented with ongoing industrial collaborations.</span>=
</p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:16.45pt;margi=
n-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.7pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:111%'><span
style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>The Ph.D. in Big Data Analytics, Statistics t=
rack,
requires 72 hours beyond an earned Bachelor's degree. Required coursework
includes<span style=3D'letter-spacing:2.0pt'> </span>30 credit hours of req=
uired
courses, 21 credit hours of restricted elective coursework, and 21 credit h=
ours
of dissertation research.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:16.45pt;margi=
n-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>All Ph.D. students must have an
approved Plan of Study (POS) developed by the student and advisor that lists
the specific courses to be taken as part of the degree. Students must maint=
ain
a minimum GPA of 3.0 in their POS, as well as a &quot;B&quot; (3.0) in all
courses completed toward the degree and since admission to the program.</sp=
an></p>

