style=3D'letter-spacing:-.1pt;mso-font-width:120%'> Description</span><span
style=3D'text-decoration:none;text-underline:none'><o:p></o:p></span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:8.45pt;margin-right:16.45pt;marg=
in-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>The Feature Film Production MFA i=
s a
terminal degree, the highest degree awarded to filmmakers or film artists. =
It
is a rigorous professional film production program for film practitioners a=
nd
visual artists who demonstrate a commitment to the expressive potential of
filmmaking and the exploration of non-traditional modes of distribution. The
Feature Film Production MFA produces graduates<span style=3D'letter-spacing=
:.55pt'>
</span>with<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>mastery<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>of<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55p=
t'> </span>storytelling<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>through<span style=3D'letter-spacing=
:.55pt'>
</span>cinema<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>as<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>it<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55p=
t'> </span>encourages<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>the<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55=
pt'> </span>candidate<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>to<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55p=
t'> </span>find<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>a<span style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt=
'> </span>personal<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>style.<span style=3D'letter-spacing:=
.55pt'> </span>The<span
style=3D'letter-spacing:.55pt'> </span>program emphasizes story, performanc=
e,
aesthetic choice, business, and creative thinking. The program develops
graduates who can compete<span style=3D'letter-spacing:2.0pt'> </span>in the
worlds of national and international independent filmmaking.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:12.2pt;margin=
-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>Students will pursue a modality
&#8211;narrative, documentary, or experimental&#8211; for their thesis film=
, or
body of work, during their first two semesters in the program. All MFA
candidates must take the core required courses but will choose electives th=
at
best match their modalities and interests. Upon completion of the degree, e=
ach
student will have produced a micro-budget digital feature film or equivalent
body of work that meets standards outlined in the Program Graduate Handbook.
Students will also have prepared a marketing strategy for its distribution =
and
exhibition. Graduates in this program are responsible for funding their own
thesis projects, including fundraising and soliciting investors where neede=
d.
Historically, graduates have produced feature films within the budget range=
 of
5-25K. Budgetary needs can vary greatly depending on the scope and modality=
 of
the thesis.</span></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.45pt;margin-right:19.55pt;marg=
in-bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>Consulting with the thesis commit=
tee
regarding the appropriate budgetary scale is advised for all students. Budg=
ets
exceeding 50K are strongly discouraged.</span></p>

