<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:0in;margin-right:16.45pt;margin-=
bottom:
0in;margin-left:24.75pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-.05pt;line-heigh=
t:
111%'><span style=3D'mso-font-width:110%'>We continue to improve the curric=
ulum
to adapt to the changing professional and societal demands and to offer the
best graduate education and training in human factors and cognitive psychol=
ogy.
In particular, we have modified our curriculum and program requirements and
introduced project and outcome-based competency assessments. These changes =
have
helped to focus students' attention on their respective programs of research
while simultaneously developing the knowledge and skill sets required to be
Ph.D. scientist/practitioners in human factors and cognitive psychology.</s=
pan></p>

