11.0pt;line-height:111%;mso-font-width:110%'>The written qualifying examina=
tion
should be completed within the first two years of the student's program. The
exam seeks to cover areas of general knowledge and discipline-specific
knowledge within the student's declared track. These questions could be rel=
ated
to the dissertation research proposal or designed to examine general knowle=
dge
and reasoning within the field. The candidate will meet with their advisory
committee at least two months prior to the examination to discuss expectati=
ons.
Committee members must clearly articulate in writing the general areas that=
 may
be examined. Any student failing the examination must repeat the examination
within six calendar months of the date of the first examination and the
examination requires a majority vote by committee members. A second failed
attempt will result in dismissal from the <span style=3D'letter-spacing:-.1=
pt'>program</span></span><span
style=3D'font-size:7.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:111%'><o:p><=
