le
engaged in or seeking professional careers in intelligence policy with a fo=
cus
on analysis of security threats or crises, both domestic and international,
through use of human, electronic and public domain intelligence sources.</s=
pan></p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText style=3D'margin-top:7.5pt;margin-right:16.45pt;margi=
